            <ArticleTitle>Physiologic assessment of ostial left circumflex coronary artery disease using a Doppler guidewire before and after rotational atherectomy facilitated angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intravascular Doppler assessment of coronary flow velocity has demonstrated the physiologic significance of intermediate stenoses and the success of coronary interventions. We describe a patient where Doppler evaluation confirmed the significance of an intermediate left circumflex ostial stenosis. We also describe the Doppler flow velocity characteristics after successful rotational atherectomy facilitated angioplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
